      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine the level of knowledge of asthma in asthmatic children's parents."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "A questionnaire was applied in asthmatic children's parents that had not taken some course about asthma, to explore the knowledge that they have about the illness. A questionnaire of the National Asthma Education Program of NIH was used. They were only questions of false or true options."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "512 questionnaires were applied finding mainly that 53.1% considered to the asthma an emotional illness, 52.5% believed that the way that parents raise their children cause the asthma, 32.8% considered that the acute episodes are not dangerous. The 39.1% ignored that it is possible to measure the lung function, 23.4% considered that the patient with asthma should not carry out exercise and 57.8% \"knew\" that the asthma in the children disappears spontaneously in the adolescence."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The level of education about asthma in the parents is insufficient, and also is wrong in almost half of them."
        }
      ]},
